3. HARVEST — https://github.com/hpcbg/harvest
   Licence: the repository ships NO licence file and its README declares none.

   NO HARVEST CODE IS PRESENT IN THIS REPOSITORY. Because the licence is
   unstated, only *concepts* were taken, and every one was re-implemented from
   scratch against a different domain:

     - a deterministic seeded task generator producing dataclasses from weighted
       templates (harvest/task_generator.py) -> wisepack_core/generator.py
     - a YAML `dynamic_events:` list of scripted plan-change disturbances
       (harvest/config.yaml) -> wisepack_core/events.py + config/scenarios/
     - scenario comparison and KPI summary tables (harvest/server.py,
       harvest/main.py) -> wisepack_core/kpi.py::compare_strategies
     - map-style rendering of a scene with event markers
       (harvest/farmview/_renderer.py) -> the SVG Digital Twin view in
       web/index.html and scripts/generate_demo_artifacts.py

   One deliberate divergence: HARVEST triggers dynamic events on a simulated
   wall clock, which suits a day-long farm simulation. WISEPACK triggers on
   workflow stage or placement index so a demonstration is identical on a fast
   laptop and a loaded CI runner.

